1. Providers
    - Providers are plugins that enable Terraform to communicate with external platforms and services through their APIs. Every resource managed by Terraform belongs to a provider.
    
2. Provider Version Requirements
    - It is a best practice to pin provider versions to ensure consistent behavior across environments.
    - versions.tf
        terraform {
            required_version = ">= 1.9.0"

            required_providers {
                aws = {
                source  = "hashicorp/aws"
                version = "~> 5.0"
                }
            }
        }
    - Explanation
        required_version specifies the compatible Terraform CLI versions.
        required_providers defines which providers are required.
        source identifies the provider registry namespace.
        version constrains the provider version to avoid unexpected upgrades.

3. Provider Configuration
    - Provider blocks configure how Terraform connects to a specific platform.
    - providers.tf
        provider "aws" {
            region  = "us-east-1"
            profile = "my-aws-profile" # Uses credentials from ~/.aws/credentials
        }
    - Explanation
        region specifies the AWS region where resources will be created.
        profile selects a named AWS CLI profile from the local credentials configuration.

4. How Providers Work
    Terraform reads the required_providers block.
    terraform init downloads the specified provider plugins.
    Provider configuration supplies authentication and connection settings.
    Resources use the configured provider to create, update, and destroy infrastructure.

5. Common Providers
    Provider	Source
    AWS	                hashicorp/aws
    Azure	            hashicorp/azurerm
    Google Cloud (GCP)	hashicorp/google
    Kubernetes	        hashicorp/kubernetes
    Helm	            hashicorp/helm
    Random	            hashicorp/random

    - Multiple Providers Example
        provider "aws" {
            region = "us-east-1"
        }

        provider "google" {
            project = "my-project-id"
            region  = "us-central1"
        }
    - Terraform can manage resources across multiple cloud platforms within the same configuration.

6. Initialize Providers
    After defining providers, run:
        terraform init
    Terraform downloads the required provider plugins and creates the .terraform/ directory along with the dependency lock file (.terraform.lock.hcl).